"## Flow: 9577\n\n- **Platform**: web\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/flows/9577\n- **Name**: Create and activate course certificate\n- **Screens Count**: 6\n- **Description**: Happy path: An instructor/admin who manages a course creates a certificate, selects a template, customizes content in an inline editor, and activates it so the system will automatically issue the certificate to students who complete the course. Entry point is the course's Certificates section (no certificates exist). Exit point is the Certificates list showing the newly active certificate. Assumptions: user is signed in with permission to manage the course (instructor/admin), working on a desktop or large tablet, and has a course context already selected.\n- **Problem**: User task (user perspective): The user wants to create and enable a completion certificate for a specific course so that students receive a certificate automatically after finishing the course. The user expects to pick or create a visual design, edit fields (title, recipient name placeholder, date, issuing organization, optional serial number), preview the result, and then activate distribution. Interface/system perspective: The UI presents an initial state when no certificates exist and exposes a control to create a new certificate. A template-selection modal guides the user to choose a base design or custom HTML. A WYSIWYG-like certificate editor exposes content fields (logo, title, subtitle, graduating-from label, date label) and a live preview. When the user finishes, the system shows an activation confirmation; activating toggles the certificate to be the single active certificate for the course and the system will auto-issue it on course completion. Result: User-perceived outcome — the certificate is created, customized, activated and visible in the course Certificates list as the active certificate. System-level outcome — certificate record is saved, marked active, and flagged to be automatically issued to eligible students on course completion.\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 358\n- **Name**:  Teachable\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/358\n- **Domain**: teachable.com\n- **Categories**: Business\n- **Description**: Sell Courses, Coaching and Digital Downloads\n\n### Steps\n\n#### Step 1: Certificates landing — empty state\n- **Screen ID**: 18fc03d0-0889-47d7-978f-3bcfe4fcf994\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/18fc03d0-0889-47d7-978f-3bcfe4fcf994\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/4b502cc9-e46f-4695-a9e1-2cdfddc11391_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Start creating a certificate for the course\n- **Action**: User clicks the New certificate (or Create new certificate) button from the Certificates section\n- **System Response**: The UI opens a modal titled 'Create a new certificate' showing template options and a custom certificate option. The rest of the page is dimmed.\n- **Page Types**: Content Management Page\n- **UX Patterns**: Empty State\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon\n- **Fonts**: San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Administrative certificates page for Liam's School showing an empty state, with a message that no certificates exist yet and prominent yellow buttons to create a new certificate, plus help links.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a dark left sidebar navigation and a white main content area containing a breadcrumb, page title, top-right action button, centered empty-state box, and an info bar below.\n  - Functions: Used to manage course certificates: navigate the certificates section, create a new certificate, and access documentation/help about certificate setup and distribution.\n\n#### Step 2: Template selection — modal (initial)\n- **Screen ID**: 062c1631-9841-4a3b-91c6-0c249bda4a00\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/062c1631-9841-4a3b-91c6-0c249bda4a00\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/5e7de78f-6a9b-4986-bd11-bdea6ad18655_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Choose a base certificate design or opt to build a custom one\n- **Action**: User reviews template thumbnails; initially no template is selected. User can cancel or proceed once a template is chosen.\n- **System Response**: Next button is disabled until the user selects a template or the custom option. Templates are presented as selectable cards.\n- **UX Patterns**: Add & Create, Templates\n- **UI Elements**: Cards & Tiles, Button, Dialog & Modal Window, Popover\n- **Fonts**: San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A centered modal titled \"Create a new certificate\" shows three certificate template thumbnails in a row, a link-like prompt to create a custom certificate, and Cancel/disabled Next buttons, with the rest of the app dimmed behind it.\n  - Layout: Centered white modal with rounded corners and shadow, stacked vertically with a title, a horizontal row of three template cards, centered helper text beneath, and bottom-right action buttons; dark sidebar navigation is visible but subdued in the background.\n  - Functions: Lets users pick a predefined certificate template or create one with liquid/HTML, then proceed with Next or dismiss the flow with Cancel.\n\n#### Step 3: Template selection — choose template\n- **Screen ID**: d9b958eb-3c61-4c60-8a8e-bbf3f59fcb64\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/d9b958eb-3c61-4c60-8a8e-bbf3f59fcb64\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/60cac834-c782-4050-ab67-273d332e78a0_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Select a specific certificate template to edit\n- **Action**: User clicks a template thumbnail (right-most template) to select it, then clicks Next\n- **System Response**: Modal closes and the certificate editor opens with the selected template loaded into the editor's live preview and editable fields.\n- **UX Patterns**: Select, Add & Create, Templates\n- **UI Elements**: Cards & Tiles, Button, Dialog & Modal Window, Popover\n- **Fonts**: San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A centered modal dialog for creating a new certificate appears over a darkened, blurred page, showing a title, subtitle, three certificate template previews, custom-certificate helper text, and Cancel/Next actions.\n  - Layout: Single-column modal with a header, a horizontal row of three template thumbnails, informational text beneath, and bottom-right action buttons; the underlying app and left sidebar are dimmed in the background.\n  - Functions: Users can choose a certificate template or create a custom one, then continue with Next or dismiss the dialog using Cancel or the close X.\n\n#### Step 4: Certificate editor — edit content and preview\n- **Screen ID**: 8d9a3f5d-dbef-4e4c-bd51-5a270b1ad1cb\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/8d9a3f5d-dbef-4e4c-bd51-5a270b1ad1cb\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/eb7bcfa4-6149-41d3-8f88-dcf22b517996_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Customize certificate content (logo, title, subtitle, graduating-from, date label, serial number) and verify appearance\n- **Action**: User uploads a logo (optional), edits text fields in the left content panel, and monitors the live preview on the right. User can use Preview or Finish when ready.\n- **System Response**: Changes are reflected in the live preview. Save status is shown (Saved). 'Preview' shows a full preview; clicking Finish triggers activation flow (validation may run before activation).\n- **UX Patterns**: Add & Create\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Tabs, Text Field, Sidebar & Drawer\n- **Fonts**: San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A certificate creation page with form inputs on the left and a live certificate preview on the right, featuring a title bar with Saved status, Preview, and Finish buttons.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a narrow left sidebar of stacked upload and text fields, and a larger right panel with a centered certificate preview beneath a top action bar.\n  - Functions: Users upload a logo, edit certificate text fields, review changes in the live preview, and use Preview or Finish to validate and finalize the certificate.\n\n#### Step 5: Activate certificate — confirmation\n- **Screen ID**: 07a4df56-1d06-435b-93c9-63550dc90bb4\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/07a4df56-1d06-435b-93c9-63550dc90bb4\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/8551fc70-b614-424b-bf93-68ab5941ec13_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Decide whether the newly created certificate should be issued automatically on course completion\n- **Action**: User clicks Finish in the editor, causing the system to display an 'Activate this certificate' confirmation modal. User chooses Activate (or Not Now).\n- **System Response**: If user clicks Activate, the system marks this certificate as active for the course; dialog closes and the user is returned to the Certificates list. If Not Now, the certificate is saved but not activated.\n- **UX Patterns**: Confirmation, Add & Create\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dialog & Modal Window, Popover\n- **Fonts**: San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A centered confirmation modal asks to activate a course completion certificate, with a title, explanatory text, and two buttons: Not Now and Activate. A close X appears in the top-right, and the dimmed background shows a certificate editor interface.\n  - Layout: Full-screen dark overlay with a centered white modal. The modal stacks a heading, body text, and two side-by-side buttons, while the blurred page behind shows a left settings panel, central preview area, and a top toolbar.\n  - Functions: The dialog confirms whether to activate certificate issuance so completed students receive it automatically. Users can cancel with Not Now or confirm with Activate, while the background editor indicates certificate customization options.\n\n#### Step 6: Certificates list — active certificate\n- **Screen ID**: bef39aec-2645-4fdc-9807-4d7a3676649d\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/bef39aec-2645-4fdc-9807-4d7a3676649d\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/2e703346-2564-414f-9d25-6581744326fa_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Confirm the certificate is active and visible in the course Certificates list\n- **Action**: User reviews the Certificates page where the newly created certificate appears in the Active certificates section; user may Preview or open more options from the certificate card.\n- **System Response**: Certificates list displays the active certificate with metadata (issued count, last updated timestamp). The certificate is now the course's single active certificate and will be issued automatically to students upon completion.\n- **Page Types**: Content Management Page\n- **UI Elements**: Cards & Tiles, Button, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon\n- **Fonts**: San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Certificate management dashboard for Liam's School with an active certificate card, preview controls, and a prominent New certificate button.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a dark left sidebar navigation and a white main content area featuring breadcrumb, heading, certificate card, and info box.\n  - Functions: Lets users review and manage certificates, preview the current design, access more actions, and create a new certificate.\n\n### Related Queries\n- create course certificate template\n- certificate template selection modal\n- pick certificate design template\n- open certificate editor preview\n- edit certificate content fields\n- activate certificate on completion\n- automatic certificate issuance settings\n- custom HTML certificate template\n- certificate activation confirmation dialog\n- manage active course certificate"
